{"uid":"4e2f3436987480d3","name":"test_an_obligation_naming_a_task_with_a_possessive_stays_open","fullName":"tests.test_petitions#test_an_obligation_naming_a_task_with_a_possessive_stays_open","historyId":"cda892fa7c0782e37e75642cf5b865a1","time":{"start":1791889700745,"stop":1791889700746,"duration":1},"description":"Task 002 (#165): the task-anchor extraction used to capture `039's`\n    verbatim (possessive apostrophe and all) instead of stopping at the id,\n    so an obligation phrased as \"Task 039's ...\" -- the possessive shape a\n    plain-English filing takes -- never resolved against `task_ids` even\n    when 039 is squarely in the current plan, and was wrongly dropped as\n    history. Stripping the possessive (and any trailing punctuation) before\n    the membership check fixes that: the obligation names a task this plan\n    still carries, so it is adjudicated, not history.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 002 (#165): the task-anchor extraction used to capture <code>039's</code><br />\nverbatim (possessive apostrophe and all) instead of stopping at the id,<br />\nso an obligation phrased as &quot;Task 039's ...&quot; -- the possessive shape a<br />\nplain-English filing takes -- never resolved against <code>task_ids</code> even<br />\nwhen 039 is squarely in the current plan, and was wrongly dropped as<br />\nhistory. Stripping the possessive (and any trailing punctuation) before<br />\nthe membership check fixes that: the obligation names a task this plan<br />\nstill carries, so it is adjudicated, not history.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791889683010,"stop":1791889683010,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"st